WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.456
This is Expedition News Network, with a classroom report looking back at the

00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:06.963
Endurance expedition.

00:00:06.963 --> 00:00:13.035
In 1914, Ernest Shackleton set out to cross Antarctica, but ice trapped his

00:00:13.035 --> 00:00:16.111
ship before that crossing could begin.

00:00:16.111 --> 00:00:21.618
As the ice damaged Endurance, the goal changed from exploring a continent to

00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:23.140
bringing people home.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:30.073
Shackleton's later account, South, describes supplies being prepared to move before the ship

00:00:30.073 --> 00:00:31.128
was abandoned.

00:00:31.128 --> 00:00:36.786
The party eventually reached Elephant Island, and six men sailed the James Caird

00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:39.191
toward South Georgia to seek help.

00:00:39.191 --> 00:00:45.814
All twenty-eight members of the Endurance party survived, although the wider expedition's separate

00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:47.909
Ross Sea party suffered losses.

00:00:47.909 --> 00:00:54.610
The original crossing was not completed, but preparation and cooperation helped make rescue

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.273
possible.
